// Window drag regions.
//
// The Vue marks the elements the window can be dragged by with Tauri's
// `data-tauri-drag-region` (the dialog's scrim, the app's title bar, the
// multiplayer dialog), and Tauri starts an OS window drag on a press there —
// only on the marked element itself, never on its children.
//
// Slint has no drag region and no window-drag method of its own, so a marked
// element calls this global instead: `WindowDrag.start()` from the press
// handler. `src/main.rs` wires it to `WindowService::drag_window()`, which
// hands the drag to the platform, exactly like Tauri does.
export global WindowDrag {
    /// Raised on a press inside a drag region. Must be answered by starting the
    /// platform's own window drag while the press is still being handled: on
    /// macOS the drag is started from the mouse event that is being dispatched.
    callback start();
}
